r."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Saying How Far a Place Is"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to know how far a place is, you can use the question: <span class=\"italic\">How far is \u2026 ?</span><br />When talking about distance, you use the <span class =\"strong\">Simple Present Tense</span>.<br/>You can reply with a specific distance if you know the answer, like <span class=\"italic\">It's 50 yards away.</span><br /><br />  In the USA, you use the Imperial system, not the metric system.<br /><br />  If a place is nearby, you use yards to say how far it is.<br />   If a place is far, you use miles to say how far it is."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Tourist</span>: Excuse me, how far is the Golden Gate Bridge?<br /> <span class =\"strong\">Ann</span>: It's 7 miles away."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Imperial System </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Metric System </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 mile \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 1.6 kilometers \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 yard \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"91 centimeters \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 foot \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"30 centimeters \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 inch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2.5 centimeters\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking About the Weather"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to know about the weather, you can ask a question using <span class =\"strong\">what</span>,  like <span class=\"italic\">What's the weather like?</span><br /><br />    You use the following words and phrases to talk about the weather."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Ann</span>: The weather is perfect today.<br />             <span class =\"strong\">Bob</span>: Yes, it's sunny and cool."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's ...\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" hot \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"engenn4le02ob03img01.jpg\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"warm \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"engenn4le02ob03img02.jpg\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cool \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"engenn4le02ob03img03.jpg\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cold \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"engenn4le02ob03img04.jpg\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"raining \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"engenn4le02ob03img05.jpg\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sunny\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"image\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"engenn4le02ob03img06.jpg\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "windy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with a lot of wind "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's quite windy by the water."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le02ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you walk in San Francisco!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ferry "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a boat or ship that transports people from one place to another "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ferry to Alcatraz leaves in 30 minutes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le02ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ride "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to travel in or on a vehicle  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ferry ride takes 30 minutes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le02ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mile "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a measure for distance in the Imperial system; 1.6 km "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Golden Gate Bridge is 7 miles away."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le02ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "yard "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a measure for distance in the Imperial system; 91 cm "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The bus stop is 50 yards away."}, {"type": "audio", "conte